ut --out receipts/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule_fixture_acceptance.json"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"e74e2d1858b5ae982235243bc5a0a2b186cf029107241b077fe6ea520527f441","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"verified_macro_body_import","family":"agent_reliability_and_safety","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"copied_non_secret_macro_body"},"component_id":"batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule","plain":"People who write guide documents may want to compare two ways of laying them out. This component is given a scoring program, three made-up tasks, and two sets of guide documents, one flat and one led by the main ideas. It scores each set on each task by the expected references it reaches and rough measures such as step count, and rejects any setting that puts the expected answers into the documents. In the example all three tasks favour the second set, though an audit shows the two sets hold different kinds of documents.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule.md","sha256":"ff1e57f6bcbc9f5eeb903ab03e6e1e509ef38427ca025c5323a2be562891455d","text":"# Run a small route-comparison simulation\n\n> **In plain terms.** People who write guide documents may want to compare two ways of laying them out. This component is given a scoring program, three made-up tasks, and two sets of guide documents, one flat and one led by the main ideas. It scores each set on each task by the expected references it reaches and rough measures such as step count, and rejects any setting that puts the expected answers into the documents. In the example all three tasks favour the second set, though an audit shows the two sets hold different kinds of documents.\n\nThis capsule runs a copied `cold_eval.py` over a public synthetic workspace. It compares two sets of navigation documents: a flat entry set and an idea-first packet with an entry packet, atlas and index. For each task, its score combines expected-reference coverage with heuristics for the first file reached, citations, next moves, unsupported claims and step count. The fixture’s three tasks all favour the idea-first packet, but the two sets contain different kinds of documents; the scorecard audit makes that asymmetry visible.\n\nA negative case changes the exercise manifest to permit injection of expected references; the claim-ceiling check rejects that setting. Injecting the expected answers into the material being scored would make the comparison self-fulfilling. A pass means the copied runner and the fixture checks ran under the stated constraints. It does not show that one route wins for real users or establish a neutral benchmark. The source digest verifies the copied file’s identity, not the validity of its scoring method.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root, with Python 3.11 or newer and the repository dependencies available:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule \\\n  run --input fixtures/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/input \\\n  --out .microcosm/component-guides/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/output \\\n  --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/acceptance.json\n```\n\nThe result includes the comparison and scorecard audit under `exercise`. It is written under `.microcosm/component-guides/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/output`; the acceptance receipt is separate. These paths do not overwrite the checked-in receipts.\n\n## Verification\n\nTests and fixtures exercise the scorecard and source-digest checks; they do not formally prove the scoring algorithm. The command above runs directly, without the shared admission gate. `make component-replays` separately runs the exported cold-eval bundle through the [Dafny-verified admission decision](../formal/replay/README.md), checking the host's observations of source and input identities, claim policy and receipt agreement.\n\n## Source\n\n[Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule.py) · [fixture input](../fixtures/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/input/) · [tests](../tests/test_batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule.py) · [sample result (historical)](../receipts/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule_result.json) · [JSON record](batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule.json).\n\nSee [HELM](https://crfm.stanford.edu/helm/index.html) for a broader approach to transparent evaluation.\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/exported_batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule_validation_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"microcosm batch10-cold-eval-honesty-capsule run --input fixtures/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule/input --out receipts/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule_fixture